{
 "note": "Declared manuscript panels and the measured crop geometry used to cut them out of the authenticated manuscript-final raster. Coordinates are absolute pixels in that raster. A region excludes SHARED chrome (figure title, headers spanning more than one panel, shared legends, shared colorbars); shared chrome is never bisected and survives only in the composite. Figures with no panel letters in the manuscript are absent and must never be given panels. This file is self-sufficient: 'trim' states the trimming policy, and every panel carries both its split rectangle and the final rectangle actually exported, so a rebuild is checkable without re-deriving anything.",
 "trim": {
  "description": "A split rectangle inherits the composite's outer margins, so it is shrunk onto its own ink and then given a small margin back. Trimming only ever removes blank rows/columns, so an exported panel is always a sub-rectangle of the manuscript composite and no plotted content can be lost.",
  "grayscale": "RGBA/LA/P composited over opaque white, then converted to 8-bit L",
  "ink_threshold": 250,
  "ink_predicate": "gray < 250",
  "margin_px": "int(min(60, max(8, round(0.01 * min(width, height)))))",
  "panel_pixels_sha256": "SHA-256 of the cropped panel's raw RGB pixel buffer (PIL Image.convert('RGB').crop(box).tobytes()). Hashing pixels rather than PNG bytes keeps the check independent of which PNG encoder or Pillow version writes the file."
 },
